WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:04.856
GTA 6 isn't even out… so how are reports
putting it over ONE BILLION dollars?!

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:09.520
Pre-orders opened June 25. But the actual
game doesn't launch until November 19!

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:18.056
The Standard Edition costs 79.99. The Ultimate
costs 99.99. That's twenty dollars more
before you even play!

00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:25.628
Now listen to this. Sensor Tower estimates
12.13 million digital pre-orders across
PlayStation and Xbox by November 13!

00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:32.512
That's an estimated 1.18 BILLION dollars!
Roughly 97 dollars per order, with about
three-quarters on PlayStation!

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:40.328
And here's why! Reuters reported that nearly
90 percent of pre-orders in an earlier
snapshot were for the 99.99 Ultimate Edition!

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:49.384
And remember GTA 5? Take-Two officially announced
it passed ONE BILLION in sales just THREE DAYS
after launch! But GTA 6's number is a pre-order estimate!

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:58.792
But here's the catch… Rockstar hasn't confirmed
this number. It's an estimate. So if the hype is
already worth this much… WHAT HAPPENS WHEN THE
GAME ACTUALLY DROPS?!

